      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Given that $y=-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{10}^{x}-1$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$ \n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{10}^{x}-1) \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{x})+{10}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{x}+{10}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
